diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index a782e135ab689faf3ed1c70a0f67b59c2564332b..251ca4963ef92f691ce95ee4e6c8090f077f418e 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -227,3 +227,49 @@ To use the PostgreSQL world, set the `WORKFLOW_TARGET_WORLD` environment variabl
 ```bash
 export WORKFLOW_TARGET_WORLD="@workflow/world-postgres"
 ```
+
+### Stable hook acceptance (experimental)
+
+`world.events.getResume(runId, resumeId)` reads a durable acceptance receipt from
+that run's event journal, or returns `undefined`. Its presence supports keyed
+`hook_received` creation through `events.create` with both `resumeId` (1–256
+characters) and `resumePayloadDigest` (64 lowercase hexadecimal characters).
+The event must include its hook token. The caller supplies the digest of its
+canonical semantic payload; World persists and compares it, rather than hashing
+serialized or encrypted transport bytes.
+
+The run lock serializes acceptance. Reusing a key with the same hook ID, token,
+and digest returns the original event, including after hook disposal or run
+completion. Reusing it with different values returns HTTP-status 422
+`WorkflowWorldError`. Distinct keys remain distinct inputs. A new acceptance
+requires a live hook belonging to the specified nonterminal run. Keyed legacy
+requests and runs are rejected. Unkeyed receives keep their existing append
+semantics and also validate hook run ownership.
+
+Receipts and their uniqueness constraint live in `workflow_events`; there is no
+second journal. Apply the standard migrations before using this API. Receipts
+last only as long as the corresponding event history. They attest durable input
+acceptance, not execution or user-visible delivery. This does not advertise the
+general lazy `hookResumeDedup` capability, and callers still enforce session
+authorization and schedule any required wake.
+
+For native lookup when the caller no longer knows the run, a keyed create may
+also supply `resumeScope` (1–256 characters). `events.getResumeByScope(scope, id)`
+returns the canonical owner's receipt, including `resumeScope`, even after hook
+disposal or completion. The native event journal uniquely binds `(scope, id)`
+to one run. A different run claiming that pair receives 422, including under
+concurrent writes. Per-run key uniqueness remains in force: replay must match
+the original scope, including whether it was absent. Different scopes can use
+the same input ID on different runs. Unscoped receipts omit `resumeScope`.
+Scope is a caller-supplied namespace, not authorization; the host derives it
+from trusted context and validates the returned owner before using the receipt.
+
+The real PostgreSQL property harness uses disposable `postgres:15-alpine`,
+standard migrations, independent child processes, a post-commit SIGKILL barrier,
+and observed PostgreSQL row-lock waits for disposal/completion races. Build the
+package and its workspace dependencies, then run from this package:
+
+```sh
+pnpm build
+pnpm exec vitest run test/hook-acceptance.test.ts
+```
